#### Case File 01 — LATIFY
**Top bar (monospace, cyan):**
`NCT05450692 · AstraZeneca · Phase III · NSCLC · OS primary endpoint: MISSED`

**Body:**
Ceralasertib + Durvalumab. 594 patients enrolled. FoundationOne CDx collected STK11 and KEAP1 status at screening. That data was not used to gate enrollment.

**Score reveal (counts up):**
```
Responding subgroup (STK11-loss/DDR-high):     0.8936  ✅
Non-responding subgroup (unselected):          0.6295  ❌
Delta:                                        +0.3658  (2.6× threshold)
```

**Closing:**
Cancer Cell published the STK11 mechanism 4 months before the trial reported failure. The answer was in the literature. The answer was in the freezer. Nobody connected them.

**Receipt:** `latify_curl_receipts.json` · Locked pre-enrollment

---

#### Case File 02 — CEACAM5
**Top bar:**
`CARMEN-LC03 · Sanofi · Phase III · NSCLC · Primary endpoints: MISSED`

**Body:**
Tusamitamab ravtansine. Enrolled unselected NSCLC with CEACAM5 IHC 2+ ≥50% — a threshold insufficiently selective. High Target-Lock score confirmed the target is real. Layer 2 was never applied.

**Closing:**
This is LATIFY in a different cancer with a different drug. Second independent confirmation of the same systematic pattern. CrisPRO encodes mechanism — not subgroup statistics. It cannot make this error.

**Receipt:** `predictions_2026_02_21.json` · Locked Feb 21, 2026

---

#### Case File 03 — PLCO
**Top bar (amber, not red — screening failure, not drug failure):**
`PLCO Trial · NCI · 78,209 women · 6 years · CA-125 annual screening`

**Body:**
The largest government ovarian cancer screening trial ever conducted. CA-125 missed 72% of cancers. 177 of 246 cancer patients never crossed the threshold across six years of annual testing.

**Velocity numbers (count up):**
```
CA-125 velocity in women developing cancer:      19.75 U/mL/month
CA-125 velocity in women who are cancer-free:     0.035 U/mL/month
```
500-fold difference. Hiding in a $30 blood test. Invisible to snapshot reading.

**Closing:**
MUC16 — the gene that produces CA-125 — is the 3rd most mutated gene in ovarian cancer. When it mutates, the tumor stops making CA-125. The threshold never fires. We proposed this explanation without sequencing a single patient.

**Receipt:** `package-plco-2010.2026-02-27/` · CDAS Project PLCO-2010

